-- DAASI-3640 | DAAS_CORE.COMP_DETAIL_FACT: the remarks column, as a table redeploy
-- (replaces the one-line ALTER that added it in UAT on 10/22; step 1 of the deployment)
--
-- Built from GET_DDL of the PROD table on 11/8, three changes:
--   CREATE OR ALTER, not CREATE OR REPLACE. CREATE OR REPLACE drops the table and
--     its 250M rows and makes a new empty one; CREATE OR ALTER changes the existing
--     table to match this definition and keeps the data. The UAT deploy is a no-op
--     (the column is already there) and proves the file matches the live table.
--   No database on the name, like the proc and dynamic table files; the deploy
--     supplies it.
--   The two WITH TAG clauses are left out. CREATE OR ALTER TABLE does not accept
--     tags, and omitting them does not remove the tags the columns carry; they stay
--     as they are (check after the UAT deploy, see below).
-- Every existing column is listed, unchanged. CREATE OR ALTER drops a column that
-- is missing from the statement, with its data, so this list must stay complete.
-- New columns can only go at the end, which is where COMMENTS_EXTENDED is.
-- CREATE OR ALTER is not atomic: if the deploy fails part-way, check the table
-- before rerunning.
-- DAAS_TEMP.COMP_DETAIL_FACT_TMP needs nothing: both load procs recreate it LIKE
-- this table at the start of every run, so it inherits the column.
--
-- After the deploy (either environment), three checks:
--   SELECT COUNT(*) FROM INFORMATION_SCHEMA.COLUMNS
--   WHERE TABLE_SCHEMA = 'DAAS_CORE' AND TABLE_NAME = 'COMP_DETAIL_FACT';   -- 78
--   SELECT COUNT(*) FROM DAAS_CORE.COMP_DETAIL_FACT;                        -- unchanged
--   SELECT COLUMN_NAME, TAG_NAME, TAG_VALUE
--   FROM TABLE(INFORMATION_SCHEMA.TAG_REFERENCES_ALL_COLUMNS('DAAS_CORE.COMP_DETAIL_FACT', 'table'));
--                                              -- AUTHORIZER_ID and COMPOR_AUTHOR_NBR still tagged

